{"key":"enterprise/T1124","id":"T1124","name":"System Time Discovery","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["discovery"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"An adversary may gather the system time and/or time zone settings from a local or remote system. The system time is set and stored by services, such as the Windows Time Service on Windows or systemsetup on macOS. These time settings may also be synchronized between systems and services in an enterprise network, typically accomplished with a network time server within a domain. System time information may be gathered in a number of ways, such as…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1124","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--f3c544dc-673c-4ef3-accb-53229f1ae077","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.724Z","source_object_version":"1.5","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0034","name":"Process Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0034","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--ee575f4a-2d4f-48f6-b18b-89067760adc1","page":"telemetry/DC0034/"},{"id":"DC0001","name":"Scheduled Job Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0001","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--f42df6f0-6395-4f0c-9376-525a031f00c3","page":"telemetry/DC0001/"},{"id":"DC0005","name":"Scheduled Job Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0005","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--7b375092-3a61-448d-900a-77c9a4bde4dc","page":"telemetry/DC0005/"},{"id":"DC0002","name":"User Account Authentication","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0002","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a953ca55-921a-44f7-9b8d-3d40141aa17e","page":"telemetry/DC0002/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0151","name":"Behavior-chain, platform-aware detection strategy for T1124 System Time Discovery","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0151","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--98ae5e06-7ea5-49b9-b793-7f97b1d306b2","relationship_id":"relationship--a471c195-dbf1-4c84-a314-393189769d31"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0430","name":"Analytic 0430","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0151#AN0430","guidance":"Untrusted or unusual process/script (cmd.exe, powershell.exe, w32tm.exe, net.exe, custom binaries) queries system time/timezone (e.g., w32tm /tz, net time \\\\host, Get-TimeZone, GetTickCount API) and (optionally) is followed within a short window by time-based scheduling or conditional execution (e.g., schtasks /create, at.exe, PowerShell Start-Sleep with large values).","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0151"},{"id":"AN0431","name":"Analytic 0431","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0151#AN0431","guidance":"A process (often spawned by a shell, interpreter, or malware implant) executes time discovery via commands (date, timedatectl, hwclock, cat /etc/timezone, /proc/uptime) or direct syscalls (time(), clock_gettime) and is (optionally) followed by scheduled task creation/modification (crontab, at) or conditional sleep logic.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0151"},{"id":"AN0432","name":"Analytic 0432","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0151#AN0432","guidance":"Process/script execution of systemsetup -gettimezone, date, ioreg, or API usage (timeIntervalSinceNow, gettimeofday) followed by time-based scheduling (launchd plist modification) or sleep-based execution.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0151"},{"id":"AN0433","name":"Analytic 0433","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0151#AN0433","guidance":"Interactive or remote shell/API invocation of esxcli system clock get or querying time parameters via hostd/vpxa shortly followed by time/ntp configuration checks or scheduled task creation, executed by non-standard accounts or outside maintenance windows.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0151"},{"id":"AN0434","name":"Analytic 0434","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0151#AN0434","guidance":"Non-standard or rare users/locations issue CLI commands like \"show clock detail\" or \"show timezone\"; optionally followed by configuration of time/timezone or NTP sources. AAA/TACACS+ accounting and syslog correlate execution to identity, source IP, and privilege level.","platforms":["Network Devices"],"strategy_id":"DET0151"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"